@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-hourly-rentals-eligibility-pricing-scope
+type: decision-log
+title: "Hourly rentals: eligibility, pricing, scope"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Customers must be able to rent by the hour. `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`; a rental
+shorter than a day starting and ending on the hour is priced per hour. The request does not say how
+hourly periods interact with day periods, discounts or availability.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `hourlyPrice` is an optional non-negative integer number of euro cents, validated like `dailyPrice`.
+- A request whose start and end are both UTC midnights stays a day rental. Any other request is an hourly
+  rental: start and end must be UTC whole hours, end after start, and shorter than 24 hours. An item
+  without `hourlyPrice` rejects it.
+- Total = number of hours x `hourlyPrice`. The long-rental discount does not apply (it is for 3+ days).
+- Hourly bookings use the same period overlap check as day bookings, so they clash with, and hide an
+  item from, overlapping day or hourly rentals.
+- `availability` stays a day-level query (midnights only); it was not asked to change.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Afternoon rentals are possible for items with an hourly price. Hourly availability queries are not
+supported yet. Rentals of exactly 24 hours that are not midnight-aligned remain rejected.
